    <DataNode elementId="AT2G27690-MONOMER" textLabel="AT2G27690-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9ZUX1" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, zhang">The Arabidopsis enzyme was expressed in yeast. It had highest &amp;omega;-hydroxylase activity with 9,10-epoxystearic acid, while also metabolized lauric acid (C12:0) and C18 unsaturated fatty acids. The enzyme activity with palmitic acid was low. When assayed with lauric acid, in addition to &amp;omega;-hydroxylauric acid, a dicarboxylate derivative of lauric acid was detected after prolonged incubation. It indicates that CYP94C1 is capable of oxidizing fatty acids all the way to their dicarboxylate derivatives (so called &amp;omega;-oxidation pathway).</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G27690-MONOMER" />
